{
  "summary": "Enables the -Wmissing-noreturn compiler warning flag in CMake and annotates non-returning functions, methods, and lambdas across the codebase with [[noreturn]]. It also suppresses Clang's -Wc++23-lambda-attributes warning on annotated lambdas and migrates bare C exit and abort calls (abort(), exit(), _Exit()) to their std:: counterparts in <cstdlib>.",
  "problem": "Functions that never return (such as unconditional throwers, exit handlers, and fatal assert stubs) lack [[noreturn]] annotations, which can lead to compiler analysis false positives such as spurious missing-return warnings. Without an enforced compiler warning flag, newly added non-returning functions easily omit the attribute.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"Missing [[noreturn]] attributes can cause compiler false positives and other issues; see discussion in https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35896#discussion_r3726612556.\"",
    "Commit 934c041f07 adds -Wmissing-noreturn to warning flags to enforce the attribute systematically."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Touches bundled third-party or extracted libraries (src/ipc/libmultiprocess commit marked [nomerge], and src/util/subprocess.h), which the author has submitted upstream.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Expanded the standard library refactor commit to replace bare abort() and _Exit() calls across validation, sync, and txdb with std::abort() and std::_Exit(), alongside the previous std::exit() replacements.",
  "card": "Enables the -Wmissing-noreturn compiler warning flag in CMake and annotates non-returning functions, methods, and lambdas across the codebase with [[noreturn]]. It also migrates bare C runtime abort and exit calls to std::abort, std::exit, and std::_Exit, while suppressing Clang -Wc++23-lambda-attributes warnings on annotated lambdas. This prevents compiler analysis false positives, such as spurious missing-return warnings, where the compiler cannot tell that a branch unconditionally terminates.",
